 "applies_to": "ABB ECI and ECIN integrated EC motor drives (HVAC drive), application software 2.08.",
 "summary": "The ABB ECI / ECIN drive is built onto an EC motor and connects natively to BACnet MS/TP at up to 115.2 kbps. Its object list covers run/stop, direction, fault reset and speed reference commands, drive status flags, relay and digital I/O, speed, frequency, current, power and energy readings, fault history and ramp and speed limits.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": "Application software 2.08, firmware revision 2",
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Greenheck publishes a list for its Vari-Green motor (ABB EC Titanium) with the same object names, but several instances differ (for example energy is AV 9 here and AV 8 there, Input-Reference-1 is AV 16 here and AV 14 there); use the list that matches the drive in front of you.",
  "BI 5 / BO 5 (digital output 1) are only valid when parameter 1501 is set to 0-7; with 8-10 that terminal works as an analog output.",
  "AV 0 *Output-RPM reads 0 unless the motor rated speed is entered in parameter 9908.",
  "The PICS prints the AV 9 unit as kW/h; it is the cumulative energy, listed here as kWh."
 ],
